# Skill: Responsive verification

Purpose: Validate UI changes across mobile, tablet, and desktop and ensure no layout/visibility regressions.

Viewports to test (portrait and landscape):
- iPhones: 320x568@2, 375x667@2, 375x812@3, 390x844@3, 414x896@2, 428x926@3, 440x956@3 (iPhone 17 Pro Max)
- Android phones: 360x640@3, 360x780@3, 375x812@3, 412x915@3
- Tablets: 768x1024@2, 834x1112@2, 1024x1366@2, 800x1280@2
- Desktops: 1280x800@1, 1366x768@1, 1440x900@1, 1920x1080@1, 2560x1440@1

Checks (perform for each viewport, both portrait and landscape):
1. Emulate deviceScaleFactor (DPR) and touch capability for phones/tablets.
2. No horizontal scroll is introduced.
3. Buttons & CTAs are visible and have a minimum touch target of 44x44 CSS px.
4. No clipped hint text, truncated critical copy, or hidden elements due to overflow.
5. Modals/backdrops fully cover header & bottom nav (ensure modal z-index > bottom nav).
6. Icon/thumbnail spacing and layout preserved.
7. Safe-area support: verify CSS uses env(safe-area-inset-*) where relevant (iOS notch devices).
8. Orientation support: test both portrait and landscape rotations.
9. Accessibility basics: alt text for images and label associations for inputs; basic color contrast checks.
10. Auto-scroll lists/logs: ensure auto-scroll to latest without exposing scrollbars.

Output (structured):
- Per-viewport pass/fail summary.
- For each failure: selector, severity (blocker/major/minor), short explanation.
- Suggested minimal fix (Tailwind class or 1–3 lines of code).
- Screenshot artifacts for each failing viewport.

Notes:
- Prefer fluid sizing and responsive utilities; avoid hard-coded absolute widths where they break at narrow viewports.
- When animating/translating elements (rings, progress circles), separate transform used for centering from rotation/scale animations by nesting elements.

